Third-party code in src/port/i386
=================================

Four files in this folder are copied byte for byte from other projects and
are not changed: memcpy.s, memmove.s and memset.s from musl, and memcmp.S
from newlib. They keep their names, and memcmp.S keeps its notice. The other
files are libterae's own, carry libterae's notice, and adapt them:
port_memcpy.S, port_memset.S and port_memcmp.S, which are the files
assembled, and i386mach.h, which stands in for newlib's header of the same
name. No newlib header is used.

port_memcpy.S provides both memcpy and memmove, because musl's memmove.s
jumps to __memcpy_fwd, which memcpy.s defines. There is no port_memmove.S.

